# Tolerances for a shifted cohesive zone model against the interface-fitted one between bulk
# materials of very different stiffness. Each element cut by the interface takes the material of
# the side that holds most of it, so the material boundary follows the zigzag surrogate interface
# rather than the true one. This first-order error in the mesh size changes the reaction by about
# 4 percent and the average traction by about 9 percent on the 20 x 20 mesh, and halves on the
# 40 x 40 mesh. The maximum and minimum change by up to about 1.5 percent. The floor only applies
# to the zero initial state.
GLOBAL VARIABLES relative 0 floor 0
    time relative 0 floor 0
    react_x relative 5e-2 floor 1e-6
    normal_traction_average relative 1e-1 floor 1e-6
    normal_traction_max relative 2e-2 floor 1e-6
    normal_traction_min relative 2e-2 floor 1e-6
